Project 0 — Developer Toolkit
Create a small CLI that reads configuration, processes JSON/CSV, logs results, handles invalid input, and has unit tests. Add a GitHub repository, README, setup instructions, and CI check.
Exit criteria: You can explain how the program runs, debug a failure, write tests, use Git without fear, and explain basic HTTP/SQL behavior.
PHASE 1 — Java Mastery and Python Engineering
Suggested duration: Weeks 4–12. Learn both languages, but do not try to master every advanced feature immediately.
Track A: Java as the enterprise engineering language
Learn in order
Types, control flow, methods, arrays, strings and collections
Classes, constructors, interfaces, inheritance, polymorphism and composition
Exceptions, generics, enums, records and immutability
Collections framework, equals/hashCode, ordering and comparators
Lambdas, streams, functional interfaces and Optional
Packages, modules awareness, annotations and reflection fundamentals
JVM fundamentals: bytecode, class loading, stack/heap, garbage collection and memory
Concurrency: threads, executors, synchronization, locks, futures and CompletableFuture
Race conditions, deadlocks, thread safety, Java Memory Model
Virtual threads and their use cases; profiling and performance fundamentals
Maven or Gradle, code formatting, static analysis and dependency management
JUnit 5, Mockito, test fixtures, parameterized tests, coverage and test design
