RabbitMQ exchanges, queues, bindings and routing keys
Acknowledgments, retries, backoff, dead-letter queues and recovery
Event contracts and schema evolution
At-most-once, at-least-once and practical idempotent processing
Transactional outbox and duplicate-message handling
Do not assume end-to-end exactly-once behavior across an entire application; define guarantees and recovery behavior explicitly.
