LLM evaluation
Evaluate separately:
Retrieval: recall@k, precision@k, ranking quality and source relevance
Answer: correctness, groundedness, completeness, citation quality and appropriate abstention
Operational behavior: latency, error rate, token use, cost, rate-limit behavior and fallback quality
Security: prompt injection, access control, data leakage, tool authorization and tenant isolation
Regression: compare prompt/model/index changes against a versioned golden dataset
Do not rely solely on an LLM judge. Combine automated checks, deterministic assertions, curated human-reviewed examples and domain-specific criteria.
Project 12 — QA Knowledge Assistant
RAG over sample requirements, API specifications, test plans and synthetic defects. Include source citations, document updates, access controls, retrieval comparisons, evaluation data, latency/cost measurements and a clear abstention behavior.
Project 13 — LLM Evaluation Platform
Version datasets, prompts and model configurations; run evaluation suites; score outputs; store results; compare model/prompt changes; detect regressions; block releases when critical quality/security gates fail.
Project 14 — AI Failure Analysis Platform
Ingest test results, logs and failure metadata; cluster similar failures; retrieve historical defects and documentation; generate evidence-based summaries; cite sources; present possible causes with confidence/limitations; keep engineers in control of final diagnosis.
