PHASE 13 — FLAGSHIP CAPSTONE: AI QUALITY ENGINEERING PLATFORM
This is the central portfolio project that connects your QA background to AI engineering, production software and FDE work. Build it incrementally rather than attempting the entire platform at once.
Suggested architecture
UI: React + TypeScript (optional at first; CLI/API MVP is sufficient)
API: Python + FastAPI + Pydantic
Existing test adapters: Playwright, Selenium, REST Assured, pytest, then JUnit/TestNG/Cucumber as time permits
Storage: PostgreSQL; pgvector when semantic retrieval is needed
AI: one hosted LLM API first; add another provider only when provider comparison is useful
ML: scikit-learn for baseline failure classification
Evaluation: pytest + versioned golden datasets + custom evaluation harness
Deployment: Docker, GitHub Actions, AWS, Terraform
Observability: structured logs, OpenTelemetry, metrics and dashboards
Security: IAM/roles, managed secrets, backend authorization, audit logs and safe data handling
Delivery stages
MVP 1 — Test-result ingestion
Ingest synthetic test execution JSON/CSV
Validate schema and required fields
Store runs, tests, errors, durations and metadata
Add filtering, summaries, API tests and CLI reporting
MVP 2 — Failure classification
Normalize errors and stack traces
Group duplicate/similar failures
Add deterministic rules and a simple ML baseline
Measure precision/recall and review false positives
Keep human review in the loop
MVP 3 — RAG over historical failures
Index sample defects, requirements, API docs and test documentation
Implement chunking, metadata and access rules
Return cited source passages
Compare retrieval strategies and maintain evaluation data
Abstain when evidence is insufficient
MVP 4 — LLM evaluation service
Version prompts, datasets, models and expected criteria
Test correctness, groundedness, citation quality, safety and structured output
Measure latency, token usage and cost
Run regression evaluations in CI
Block releases on critical failures
MVP 5 — Controlled diagnostic workflow/agent
Read-only tools first: search failure records, retrieve docs, summarize evidence
Tool allowlists, schema validation, permission checks and execution budgets
Audit each tool call and result
Human approval before consequential actions
Test direct/indirect prompt injection, tenant isolation and tool abuse
MVP 6 — Production readiness
Containerize and deploy to AWS
Secure credentials using managed secrets/IAM
Add CI/CD, test gates, monitoring, alerting and rollback
Test failure recovery, timeouts, rate limits, provider outages and database failures
Document threat model, architecture decisions, operational runbook, limitations and costs
Required capstone evidence
Working documented REST API
RAG with source-grounded answers
Validated structured outputs and controlled tool use
Versioned evaluation dataset
Separate retrieval and answer-quality metrics
Unit, integration, API, regression and security tests
Containerized deployment
Secure secrets and document permissions
Error/latency/usage/cost monitoring
Failure recovery and rollback
Architecture diagram, threat model and ADRs
README, demo, sample data and reproducible setup
