AI for anomaly detection, predictive maintenance, failure classification, yield prediction, test optimization, log analysis, RCA assistance, intelligent test selection and RAG over hardware docs
Eight semiconductor/system projects
C++ Hardware Test Automation Framework: Python CLI → orchestrator → C++ test engine → HAL → mock device → result collector → SQLite/PostgreSQL → dashboard; YAML/JSON, logging, parallelism and CI/CD.
DRAM/HBM Validation Simulator: simulate channels/banks/rows/columns, read/write, refresh, ECC, latency, bandwidth, randomized/sequential stress and injected errors; report test ID, latency, bandwidth, errors, ECC corrections, failure rate, simulated temperature and duration.
PCIe Validation Framework: Linux device discovery/config/link information, throughput, simulated error injection, stress, logs and reports.
Semiconductor Yield Analytics: synthetic wafer/lot/station/test-item/failure-code/bin/yield/duration dataset → Python ETL → SQL → statistics/anomaly detection → dashboard.
AI Failure Analysis: parse test/system/kernel logs, feature extraction, clustering/anomaly detection, LLM/RAG potential RCA with engineer review.
HIL Test Framework Simulator: controller → Python → C++ driver → mock hardware → UART/SPI/I2C simulation → telemetry; retries, timeouts, corrupt data, resets and recovery.
High-Performance Memory Benchmark: C++ sequential/random read/write, latency/throughput, multithreading, CPU/cache; Python analysis.
Semiconductor CI/CD Platform: GitHub → PR → build → C++ unit tests → Python tests → static analysis → performance → hardware simulation → results/dashboard.
Semiconductor certification options
C++ Institute/vendor-neutral C++ credentials (practical projects matter more)
Linux Foundation or LPIC-1
ISTQB CTFL and relevant advanced/technical testing modules: https://www.istqb.org/
AWS Developer Associate or SAA
NVIDIA DLI/CUDA learning: https://developer.nvidia.com/educator-programs
NVIDIA CUDA documentation: https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/
Semiconductor learning order
Modern C++ → CMake/GoogleTest → Linux systems programming → GDB/Valgrind/sanitizers/perf → computer architecture → digital logic → UART/SPI/I2C/GPIO → networking/PCIe → semiconductor fundamentals → DRAM/DDR → HBM → memory controllers/ECC → SoC validation → ATE/testing → yield analytics → HIL automation → AI failure analysis.
