PHASE 20 — WEEKLY STUDY ROUTINE
For 10–12 hours per week:
3 hours: concepts and official documentation
3–4 hours: coding exercises and implementation
3 hours: project development
1–2 hours: tests, debugging, review and communication practice
Example 12-hour schedule:
Monday: concepts — 1.5 hours
Tuesday: coding — 1.5 hours
Wednesday: DSA/SQL or debugging — 1.5 hours
Thursday: project implementation — 2 hours
Friday: tests/refactoring — 1.5 hours
Saturday: deep project work — 3 hours
Sunday: review and communication — 1 hour
FDE 11-hour alternative:
Monday: learning — 1.5 hours
Tuesday: coding — 1.5 hours
Wednesday: documentation/debugging — 1.5 hours
Thursday: project implementation — 1.5 hours
Friday: tests/refactoring — 1 hour
Saturday: project milestone — 3 hours
Sunday: review/communication — 1 hour
Use a 70/20/10 learning allocation as a guideline: roughly 70% building and debugging, 20% reading/review/feedback, 10% structured courses. Adapt it to the phase.
PHASE 21 — FIRST 30 DAYS: START HERE
Week 1 — Python and test-result CLI
Install/use a Python environment, Git and a code editor
Learn variables, collections, functions, files and exceptions
Parse synthetic CSV/JSON test results
Produce a summary report and meaningful exit codes
Add a README and sample input
Week 2 — Modular code and testing
Split parsing, validation, reporting and configuration into modules
Add Pydantic models or explicit schema validation
Add logging and useful error messages
Add pytest fixtures, parametrization and edge cases
Add type hints and format/lint checks
Week 3 — HTTP, REST and FastAPI
Learn request/response, methods, status codes, JSON, timeout/retry concepts
Create FastAPI endpoints to upload/list test runs
Add OpenAPI docs, validation and API tests
Mock external services; never call employer systems without authorization
Week 4 — PostgreSQL and project structure
Create a PostgreSQL schema for test runs, cases and results
Add migrations and transaction handling
Add database integration tests
Create an architecture diagram, setup instructions and CI workflow
Record what is incomplete and plan the next month
First-30-day result: A tested, documented Test Execution Intelligence CLI/API—not a perfect platform.
