Portfolio standards
Every selected project should include:
Clear problem statement and target user
Requirements, assumptions and non-goals
Architecture diagram and data flow
Reproducible setup and sample data
Automated tests and CI
Security considerations and threat model where relevant
Performance/evaluation evidence
Failure scenarios and recovery behavior
Known limitations and future improvements
Demo and concise README
FINAL RECOMMENDATION
Your best route is not to become a beginner in ten technologies at the same time. Use Java/Spring Boot/PostgreSQL to strengthen software engineering, use Python/FastAPI for AI and FDE delivery, and build the AI Quality Engineering Platform as the long-running project that connects both worlds.
Priority order:
Programming and engineering fundamentals
Java + Python + testing + SQL
APIs, backend and data modeling
DSA, design, concurrency and debugging
Messaging, distributed systems and architecture
Cloud, CI/CD, security and observability
Full-stack delivery
Math and classical ML
LLMs, RAG and evaluation
Agents/MCP, AI security and governance
MLOps and production GenAI
FDE customer discovery, deployment and communication
Flagship capstone and interview readiness
Optional advanced tracks selected for the target role
Build → deploy → break safely → debug → measure → secure → explain. That loop will make the knowledge durable and help turn courses into demonstrated engineering capability.